hecks use absolute edge counts. Failures are reported with $error, and the testbench ends with the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict and $finish.", "entry": "tb_axil_timer"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["No lint, simulation, synthesis or formal tool was run by this seat. The lint-clean, latch-free and simulation-pass properties are intended, not shown.", "The testbench's per-cycle reference model was written from interface spec section 7.1 and has the same priority structure as the RTL. A defect shared by both would not be caught by the model alone. The directed checks with absolute edge counts (E+N end, stop-edge decrement, CTRL-wins, end-beats-clear, read on the same edge, 2-edge throughput) are the independent part.", "The TMR-LOAD-END-EDGE open choice (LOAD write on a periodic end edge) is implemented as old-LOAD reload but is deliberately not exercised by the testbench, so no test depends on an open choice (TMR-TEST-RANGE).", "The `ifdef FORMAL` immediate assertions in the RTL are design intent only. No formal_spec is submitted, so they are not proven, and they hold only after reset.", "The hand check of next-state equations upstream is unsubstantiated [evidence:prj-ada3a9b9d9.microarchitecture.e1]. The inputs were approved by harness rule only [evidence:prj-ada3a9b9d9.microarchitecture.e4]."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Decisions to review:\n\n- **Formal proof:** no formal_spec was produced, so formal.run and formal.cover do not apply.\n- **Second ADDR_WIDTH value:** the testbench uses 8 as the value above 4. For width 4, only misaligned addresses are unmapped. For width 8, offsets 0x10, 0x14, 0x40 and 0xFC are checked as SLVERR, with no aliasing.\n- **Simulator dependency:** the testbench assumes an Icarus-style simulator that supports $error and $value$plusargs. It uses no `timescale`.\n\nRisks the platform checks may surface:\n\n- Verilator -Wall warnings I did not anticipate, such as the `(wa >> 4)` compare at ADDR_WIDTH 4.\n- A timing slip in the testbench's direct